From: itsdunintime104 <270179414+itsdunintime104@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:53:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Mac: a Fullscreen resolution setting caps the drawable in
 fullscreen (DM_OUTPUT_HEIGHT)

In fullscreen the drawable follows the screen's own pixels: 4112x2580 on a 16-inch MacBook Pro in a scaled desktop mode. Ocarina of Time's docked picture is 2560x1440, so the present scales it up on the GPU to a drawable far larger than the picture.

DM_OUTPUT_HEIGHT=<n> keeps the fullscreen drawable at the size where the 16:9 picture is n pixels high (1440 or 1080 in the settings window), and the compositor scales it to the screen. 0 or unset keeps the screen's own pixels, and a window always keeps its own. The two fullscreen observers call fitDrawable, so the cap is evaluated again when a transition is over.

Checked on an M1 Max with Ocarina of Time: with 1080 the log shows "front end: drawable 1920x1205 (DM_OUTPUT_HEIGHT)" in fullscreen, and a window was not capped. test_launcher_settings covers the row. With a cap below the game's picture MetalFX presenting does nothing: the picture is scaled down.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Ocarina of Time on a high-resolution Mac screen: a fullscreen size the player picks, so the GPU does not fill the screen's own pixels
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#929

